  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "03fd6907",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Hyperparameter Tuning"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eca2d178",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Model Selection\n",
    "\n",
    "zu testen:\n",
    "LogRegCV |\n",
    "LogRegEN |\n",
    "RF |\n",
    "SVM |\n",
    "?KNN?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "38f09739",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Modelle definieren & trainieren\n",
    "Mit Pipeline: \"Pipeline allows you to sequentially apply a list of transformers to preprocess the data and, if desired, conclude the sequence with a final predictor for predictive modeling.\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 43,
   "id": "27e73fec",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "PREPROCESSING = [\n",
    "    (\"variance\", VarianceThreshold()),\n",
    "    (\"select\",   SelectKBest(score_func=f_classif, k=best_k)),\n",
    "    (\"scaler\",   StandardScaler()),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "cv_strategy = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "45bfa5c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 1) Logistic Regression mit L2-Regularisierung"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 44,
   "id": "8d4ee953",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Trainiere LogReg L2 ...\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "c:\\Users\\niels\\miniconda3\\envs\\fods\\Lib\\site-packages\\sklearn\\linear_model\\_logistic.py:1780: FutureWarning: The default value for l1_ratios will change from None to (0.0,) in version 1.10. From version 1.10 onwards, only array-like with values in [0, 1] will be allowed, None will be forbidden. To avoid this warning, explicitly set a value, e.g. l1_ratios=(0,).\n",
      "  warnings.warn(\n",
      "c:\\Users\\niels\\miniconda3\\envs\\fods\\Lib\\site-packages\\sklearn\\linear_model\\_logistic.py:1811: FutureWarning: 'penalty' was deprecated in version 1.8 and will be removed in 1.10. To avoid this warning, leave 'penalty' set to its default value and use 'l1_ratios' instead. Use l1_ratios=(0,) instead of penalty='l2'  and l1_ratios=(1,) instead of penalty='l1'.\n",
      "  warnings.warn(\n",
      "c:\\Users\\niels\\miniconda3\\envs\\fods\\Lib\\site-packages\\sklearn\\linear_model\\_logistic.py:1823: FutureWarning: The fitted attributes of LogisticRegressionCV will be simplified in scikit-learn 1.10 to remove redundancy. Set`use_legacy_attributes=False` to enable the new behavior now, or set it to `True` to silence this warning during the transition period while keeping the deprecated behavior for the time being. The default value of use_legacy_attributes will change from True to False in scikit-learn 1.10. See the docstring of LogisticRegressionCV for more details.\n",
      "  warnings.warn(\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  Bestes C: 0.0139\n",
      "  Fertig.\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── 1) Logistic Regression L2 ────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "pipe_lr = Pipeline(PREPROCESSING + [\n",
    "    (\"model\", LogisticRegressionCV(\n",
    "        Cs=np.logspace(-3, 1, 8),\n",
    "        cv=5,\n",
    "        penalty=\"l2\",\n",
    "        solver=\"lbfgs\",\n",
    "        scoring=\"balanced_accuracy\",\n",
    "        class_weight=\"balanced\",\n",
    "        max_iter=2000,\n",
    "        random_state=42,\n",
    "        n_jobs=-1\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Trainiere LogReg L2 ...\")\n",
    "pipe_lr.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "print(f\"  Bestes C: {pipe_lr.named_steps['model'].C_[0]:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(\"  Fertig.\\n\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a2e8a29f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 2) Logistic Regression mit Elastic Net"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 45,
   "id": "01cd61bc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Trainiere Elastic Net ...\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "c:\\Users\\niels\\miniconda3\\envs\\fods\\Lib\\site-packages\\sklearn\\linear_model\\_logistic.py:1811: FutureWarning: 'penalty' was deprecated in version 1.8 and will be removed in 1.10. To avoid this warning, leave 'penalty' set to its default value and use 'l1_ratios' instead. Use l1_ratios=(0,) instead of penalty='l2'  and l1_ratios=(1,) instead of penalty='l1'.\n",
      "  warnings.warn(\n",
      "c:\\Users\\niels\\miniconda3\\envs\\fods\\Lib\\site-packages\\sklearn\\linear_model\\_logistic.py:1823: FutureWarning: The fitted attributes of LogisticRegressionCV will be simplified in scikit-learn 1.10 to remove redundancy. Set`use_legacy_attributes=False` to enable the new behavior now, or set it to `True` to silence this warning during the transition period while keeping the deprecated behavior for the time being. The default value of use_legacy_attributes will change from True to False in scikit-learn 1.10. See the docstring of LogisticRegressionCV for more details.\n",
      "  warnings.warn(\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  Bestes C:        0.1931\n",
      "  Bestes l1_ratio: 0.10\n",
      "  Fertig.\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── 2) Logistic Regression Elastic Net ───────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "pipe_en = Pipeline(PREPROCESSING + [\n",
    "    (\"model\", LogisticRegressionCV(\n",
    "        Cs=np.logspace(-3, 1, 8),\n",
    "        cv=5,\n",
    "        penalty=\"elasticnet\",\n",
    "        solver=\"saga\",\n",
    "        l1_ratios=[0.1, 0.5, 0.9],\n",
    "        scoring=\"balanced_accuracy\",\n",
    "        class_weight=\"balanced\",\n",
    "        max_iter=3000,\n",
    "        random_state=42,\n",
    "        n_jobs=-1\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Trainiere Elastic Net ...\")\n",
    "pipe_en.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "print(f\"  Bestes C:        {pipe_en.named_steps['model'].C_[0]:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Bestes l1_ratio: {pipe_en.named_steps['model'].l1_ratio_[0]:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(\"  Fertig.\\n\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a6dea2a0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 3) Random Forest"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 46,
   "id": "d5fe0c4e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Trainiere Random Forest ...\n",
      "  Fertig.\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── 3) Random Forest ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "pipe_rf = Pipeline(PREPROCESSING + [\n",
    "    (\"model\", RandomForestClassifier(\n",
    "        n_estimators=best_k,\n",
    "        max_features=\"sqrt\",\n",
    "        class_weight=\"balanced\",\n",
    "        random_state=42,\n",
    "        n_jobs=-1\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Trainiere Random Forest ...\")\n",
    "pipe_rf.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "print(\"  Fertig.\\n\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eae7732b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
