  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e725f8e9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Feature Importance --> Wichtigste Gene"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d691f778",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Je nach Modelltyp unterscheidet sich die Interpretation:\n",
    "- **LogReg / Elastic Net**: Koeffizienten zeigen, welche Gene für welchen Subtyp sprechen\n",
    "- **Random Forest**: Feature Importance (Gini) zeigt globale Wichtigkeit über alle Subtypen\n",
    "- **SVM**: Koeffizientenvektor des linearen Kernels (entspricht den Gewichten der Hyperebene)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 52,
   "id": "ac3c3694",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Feature-Analyse für: Elastic Net\n",
      "\n",
      "Top 5 Gene pro Subtyp (nach absolutem Koeffizienten):\n",
      "  Basal: ['ZNF454', 'FOXC1', 'GDF5', 'GFRA3', 'ATL2']\n",
      "  Her2: ['ESR1', 'FLJ45983', 'TRIM3', 'CCDC125', 'C6orf97']\n",
      "  LumA: ['BCL2', 'RANBP1', 'NAT1', 'PIF1', 'FOXC1']\n",
      "  LumB: ['PPP1R14C', 'SCUBE2', 'GFAP', 'C6orf97', 'PDGFD']\n",
      "  Normal: ['OXTR', 'GLRA4', 'KCNMB1', 'CNN1', 'NAT1']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── Feature Importance des besten Modells ─────────────────────────────────\n",
    "best_name  = comparison.iloc[0][\"Modell\"]          # z.B. \"Elastic Net\"\n",
    "best_pipe  = results[best_name][\"pipe\"]             # die ganze Pipeline\n",
    "best_clf   = best_pipe.named_steps[\"model\"]         # nur der Classifier\n",
    "\n",
    "# Gennamen nach VarianceThreshold + SelectKBest rekonstruieren\n",
    "var_mask    = best_pipe.named_steps[\"variance\"].get_support()\n",
    "select_mask = best_pipe.named_steps[\"select\"].get_support()\n",
    "selected_genes = X_train.columns[var_mask][select_mask]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Feature-Analyse für: {best_name}\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if best_name in (\"LogReg L2\", \"Elastic Net\"):\n",
    "    coef_df = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "        best_clf.coef_,\n",
    "        index=best_clf.classes_,\n",
    "        columns=selected_genes\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    print(\"Top 5 Gene pro Subtyp (nach absolutem Koeffizienten):\")\n",
    "    for subtype in best_clf.classes_:\n",
    "        top5 = coef_df.loc[subtype].abs().sort_values(ascending=False).head(5)\n",
    "        print(f\"  {subtype}: {list(top5.index)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "elif best_name == \"Random Forest\":\n",
    "    importances = pd.Series(\n",
    "        best_clf.feature_importances_,\n",
    "        index=selected_genes\n",
    "    ).sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "    print(\"Top 10 Gene (Random Forest Feature Importance):\")\n",
    "    print(importances.head(10).to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "elif best_name == \"SVM (linear)\":\n",
    "    # best_clf ist hier ein GridSearchCV-Objekt → .best_estimator_ holt die SVC\n",
    "    svc = best_clf.best_estimator_\n",
    "    coef_df = pd.DataFrame(svc.coef_, columns=selected_genes)\n",
    "    print(\"Top 5 Gene mit grössten absoluten SVM-Gewichten (alle Klassen):\")\n",
    "    top_genes = coef_df.abs().max(axis=0).sort_values(ascending=False).head(5)\n",
    "    print(top_genes.to_string())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "382a6074",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Bestes Modell trainieren"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "de6f5386",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "aufpassen, dass Testset noch nicht gesehen\n",
    "möglicherweise mit crossvalidation verbessern?\n",
    "--> neues modell\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "91cdc715",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Warum ein neues Modell und nicht einfach pipe_en verwenden?\n",
    " → Im Modellvergleich haben wir die Testset-Metriken aller 4 Modelle gesehen und anhand davon Elastic Net ausgewählt. Damit sind die Testdaten indirekt in die Modellauswahl eingeflossen (sog. \"implicit leakage\"). --> Um eine wirklich unverfälschte finale Zahl zu erhalten, setzen wir das Modell neu auf – mit denselben Hyperparametern, aber so, als hätten wir die Testdaten nie gesehen.\n",
    "\n",
    "Woher kommen die Hyperparameter (C, l1_ratio)?\n",
    "--> pipe_en hat intern via 5-Fold Cross Validation auf X_train die besten Werte gesucht. Diese CV-Ergebnisse sind sauber (kein Testset involviert), daher übernehmen wir C und l1_ratio direkt daraus."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 53,
   "id": "af7c27bc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Übernommene Hyperparameter aus CV:\n",
      "  C        = 0.1931\n",
      "  l1_ratio = 0.10\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Beste Hyperparameter aus dem CV-Vergleich auslesen\n",
    "# pipe_en.named_steps[\"model\"] ist das LogisticRegressionCV-Objekt\n",
    "best_C        = results[\"Elastic Net\"][\"pipe\"].named_steps[\"model\"].C_[0]\n",
    "best_l1_ratio = results[\"Elastic Net\"][\"pipe\"].named_steps[\"model\"].l1_ratio_[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Übernommene Hyperparameter aus CV:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  C        = {best_C:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  l1_ratio = {best_l1_ratio:.2f}\")\n",
    "print()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 54,
   "id": "aeabaaf1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Finales Modell definieren ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# Identisches Preprocessing wie im Vergleich (VarianceThreshold → SelectKBest → Scaler)\n",
    "# Jetzt aber LogisticRegression (nicht CV-Variante), weil die Hyperparameter\n",
    "# bereits feststehen und nicht mehr gesucht werden müssen.\n",
    "\n",
    "final_pipe = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"variance\", VarianceThreshold()),                          # entfernt konstante Gene\n",
    "    (\"select\",   SelectKBest(score_func=f_classif, k=best_k)),    # top k Gene via ANOVA\n",
    "    (\"scaler\",   StandardScaler()),                             # z-Standardisierung\n",
    "    (\"model\",    LogisticRegression(\n",
    "        penalty=\"elasticnet\",\n",
    "        solver=\"saga\",\n",
    "        C=best_C,                  # bestes C aus CV\n",
    "        l1_ratio=best_l1_ratio,    # bestes l1_ratio aus CV\n",
    "        class_weight=\"balanced\",   # kompensiert Klassenimbalanz (Her2 selten)\n",
    "        max_iter=3000,\n",
    "        random_state=42\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 55,
   "id": "6cc6cc7e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Trainiere finales Modell auf X_train ...\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "c:\\Users\\niels\\miniconda3\\envs\\fods\\Lib\\site-packages\\sklearn\\linear_model\\_logistic.py:1135: FutureWarning: 'penalty' was deprecated in version 1.8 and will be removed in 1.10. To avoid this warning, leave 'penalty' set to its default value and use 'l1_ratio' or 'C' instead. Use l1_ratio=0 instead of penalty='l2', l1_ratio=1 instead of penalty='l1', and C=np.inf instead of penalty=None.\n",
      "  warnings.warn(\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  Fertig.\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── Training ausschliesslich auf Trainingsdaten ───────────────────────────────\n",
    "# X_train / y_train: die 80 % die das Modell sehen darf.\n",
    "# X_test  / y_test:  werden erst im nächsten Schritt verwendet – einmalig.\n",
    "print(\"Trainiere finales Modell auf X_train ...\")\n",
    "final_pipe.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "print(\"  Fertig.\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "final_pred_train = final_pipe.predict(X_train)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 56,
   "id": "2aa28993",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "══════════════════════════════════════════════\n",
      " FINALES MODELL --- Evaluation auf dem Testset\n",
      "══════════════════════════════════════════════\n",
      "Balanced Accuracy: 0.8953\n",
      "Accuracy: 0.8947\n",
      "\n",
      "              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n",
      "\n",
      "       Basal       0.96      0.93      0.95        28\n",
      "        Her2       0.80      0.92      0.86        13\n",
      "        LumA       0.93      0.90      0.91        87\n",
      "        LumB       0.81      0.89      0.85        38\n",
      "      Normal       0.91      0.83      0.87        24\n",
      "\n",
      "    accuracy                           0.89       190\n",
      "   macro avg       0.88      0.90      0.89       190\n",
      "weighted avg       0.90      0.89      0.90       190\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── Einmalige Evaluation auf dem Testset ─────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# Dies ist die einzige und letzte Berührung mit den Testdaten.\n",
    "# Die resultierende Balanced Accuracy ist die offizielle finale Modellleistung.\n",
    "final_pred_test = final_pipe.predict(X_test)\n",
    "final_ba   = balanced_accuracy_score(y_test, final_pred_test)\n",
    "final_accuracy = accuracy_score(y_test, final_pred_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"══════════════════════════════════════════════\")\n",
    "print(\" FINALES MODELL --- Evaluation auf dem Testset\")\n",
    "print(\"══════════════════════════════════════════════\")\n",
    "print(f\"Balanced Accuracy: {final_ba:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Accuracy: {final_accuracy:.4f}\\n\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, final_pred_test))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ebe17249",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### hierarchischer Classifier\n",
    "\n",
    "Wird auf den selben Daten trainiert wie das eigentliche Modell --> gleiche Ergebnisse --> useless"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 57,
   "id": "40eb0a3b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "c:\\Users\\niels\\miniconda3\\envs\\fods\\Lib\\site-packages\\sklearn\\linear_model\\_logistic.py:1135: FutureWarning: 'penalty' was deprecated in version 1.8 and will be removed in 1.10. To avoid this warning, leave 'penalty' set to its default value and use 'l1_ratio' or 'C' instead. Use l1_ratio=0 instead of penalty='l2', l1_ratio=1 instead of penalty='l1', and C=np.inf instead of penalty=None.\n",
      "  warnings.warn(\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "══════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n",
      " HIERARCHISCHER CLASSIFIER vs. FINALES MODELL (Balanced Accuracy)\n",
      "══════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n",
      "  Final Model (Elastic Net): 0.8953\n",
      "  Final Model + Hierarchical Classifier:    0.8976\n",
      "  Difference:                   +0.0023\n",
      "\n",
      "              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n",
      "\n",
      "       Basal       0.96      0.93      0.95        28\n",
      "        Her2       0.80      0.92      0.86        13\n",
      "        LumA       0.93      0.91      0.92        87\n",
      "        LumB       0.83      0.89      0.86        38\n",
      "      Normal       0.91      0.83      0.87        24\n",
      "\n",
      "    accuracy                           0.90       190\n",
